  "name": "Música guanacasteca (Guanacaste marimba dance music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The folk dance music of Guanacaste, Costa Rica's northwestern province around Liberia, Santa Cruz and Nicoya, which shares much with neighbouring Nicaragua: the punto guanacasteco, honoured as Costa Rica's national dance, and the tambito and parrandera dance tunes, played on the diatonic marimba with guitars. Dances pause for bombas, humorous rhymed verses called out by a dancer when the music stops. The Central American marimba card stands in for the Guanacaste marimba.",
